  m_text: "Shared locks:\r\nAllows multiple processes to read data concurrently No
    process can modify data while shared locks exist Optimizes performance for read-heavy
    workloads Compatible with other shared locks, incompatible with exclusive locks
    \nWrite locks:\r\nGrants exclusive access to a resource for modification Prevents
    all other processes from reading or writing Ensures data integrity during updates
    Incompatible with both shared and other exclusive locks\nWhich lock combination
    does NOT result in a deadlock?\n\r\n"
